					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-5763734#post-3820706</guid>
				<title>TLs&#039;s guide to apocalypse names</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-5763734/doomsday-contest#post-3820706</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 02 Jun 2018 02:04:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>TL333s</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1304786</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Gosh, these doomsdays, they have a bunch of wacky letters in 'em, don't they? Here's a quick rundown of how to say all this nonsense, for those of us bound to the English language. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Because I have no other skills</span> May be updated if more scenario names get added.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>هلاك-Class &quot;Darkbody&quot; End-of-All-Worlds Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>&quot;Halak&quot;, the Arabic word for &quot;destruction&quot;.</p> <blockquote> <p>Ϡ-Class &quot;Death-of-the-Mind's-Eye&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>Sampi, an archaic letter of the Greek alphabet.</p> <blockquote> <p>ℵK-Class &quot;Apotheosis&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>The Hebrew letter Aleph.</p> <blockquote> <p>ΩK-Class &quot;End-Of-Death&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>Probably everyone knows what an Omega is, but I'm taking no chances.</p> <blockquote> <p>ZK-λ-Class &quot;Cosmic Fragmentation&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>Similarly, that's ZK-Lambda.</p> <blockquote> <p>☿K-Class “World of Babel” Global-Incomprehension Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>This is the symbol for the planet Mercury. Or, in fitting with the Mars-for-men, Venus-for-women model, for intersex or transgender individuals.</p> <blockquote> <p>Öß-Class &quot;Multi-Universal Amalgamation&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>These are both German letters, properly &quot;O umlaut&quot; and &quot;Esszet&quot;. Ö is pronounced kind of like an English &quot;oo&quot;, but lower and more forward in the mouth. (Say &quot;ay&quot; like in &quot;cake&quot;; draw it out; then round your lips, and there you are!) ß is becoming more obsolete, as it's just a double s.</p> <blockquote> <p>ז-Class &quot;Great Religious War&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>Hebrew letter Zayin.</p> <blockquote> <p>Ω᧟-Class &quot;Doomsday Cascade&quot; Scenario</p> </blockquote> <p>That's another Omega along with Laev, a symbol from the Tai Lue language of Southeast Asia. What it <em>is</em>, I cannot fully ascertain, but as it comes at the end of their <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Tai_Lue_(Unicode_block)">Unicode block</a>, it's more likely a grammatical symbol than an actual letter. So, your guess is as good as mine. Unless you actually speak Tai Lue, in which case help. D:</p> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
